add([783,784],'learning-data-not-upload','Interpret fitting without inventing remote transfer','The shown ML code calls .fit(X_tr,y_tr); what does this mean in the displayed local example?', ['Pass the feature/label arrays to the estimator’s fitting operation; no remote upload is shown','Upload the arrays to an unspecified cloud service because every fit call requires it','Send the labels to every robot on the network','Replace the labels with the hand-written rule’s strings before fitting'],0,'The source phrase upload data in model is informal; the code contains an estimator call, not a network-transfer command.',['This follows the actual operation and avoids an unsupported transfer claim.','The displayed code specifies no remote service.','No such communication appears.','The shown fit uses the split dataset targets.'],typ='code')
