add(784,'slam-qualification','Avoid classifying every mapping system as learned','The slide lists SLAM under unsupervised examples; what qualification is necessary?', ['Mapping can include unlabeled learning, but SLAM may instead use geometric/probabilistic estimation without being an unsupervised ML algorithm','Every SLAM implementation is necessarily an unsupervised learning model','Every mapping task is necessarily supervised classification with terrain labels','Using sensors makes a system reinforcement learning regardless of its training signal'],0,'The learning category depends on the actual model and feedback, not merely on the application name SLAM.',['This preserves the illustrative role without an unsupported universal taxonomy.','SLAM includes non-learning estimation methods.','Mapping need not be classification or use supplied terrain labels.','Sensors do not by themselves define reward-based learning.'],conflict='Page784 lists SLAM as an unsupervised-learning example; this is not an intrinsic classification of every SLAM method.')
