add(786,'supervised-feature-label','Separate grasp inputs from target labels','In the grasp example, which pairing identifies features and supervised target correctly?', ['Force and slip are input features; success/failure is the target label','Success/failure is the input feature; force and slip are two target classes','Force is the class label and slip is the only training example','The blue/red background colors are raw force measurements'],0,'The dataset contains force/slip observations paired with grasp-result labels.',['This follows the stated data roles.','This reverses inputs and target.','Force is a feature, not a discrete outcome label in this formulation.','The colored regions show predicted classes rather than raw force units.'])
add(786,'grasp-boundary-figure','Read the grasp classification region','The new star lies in the blue region; with class0=success and class1=failure in this figure, what does the classifier predict?', ['Class0,success','Class1,failure','A continuous grip force equal to zero','No prediction because a new point must match a training point exactly'],0,'The star is in the region labeled class0; the numeric class label means success in this particular example.',['This uses the figure’s own class mapping.','That is the red-region mapping.','A class label0 is not a numeric force estimate.','A classifier can label a new location without exact equality to a training sample.'],typ='diagram')
add(787,'classification-regression','Distinguish class labels from measured quantities','Which pair correctly identifies classification versus regression for robot outputs?', ['Terrain type is classification; required grip force in newtons is regression','Terrain type is regression because its labels can be0,1,2; grip force is classification because it is numeric','Both are classification whenever a computer stores the outputs as numbers','Both are regression whenever the input comes from a sensor'],0,'Class labels represent categories even when encoded numerically, while force is a quantitative output.',['This distinguishes output meaning rather than storage type.','Numeric encoding does not turn a category into a continuous quantity.','Storage as numbers is not the criterion.','Input source does not determine target type.'],typ='scenario')
