add(789,'neighbor-count-boundaries','Interpret the illustrated1,3,9-neighbor boundaries','What does the side-by-side boundary comparison illustrate without proving universal performance ordering?', ['Changing k can alter boundary smoothness and predictions; a larger k is not guaranteed to improve unseen accuracy','Nine neighbors must be more accurate than three on every possible dataset','Changing k changes the number of output classes from1to3to9','All boundaries must remain identical because the stored points are unchanged'],0,'The same training set can yield different local voting behavior as k changes; suitability requires evaluation.',['This is the bounded interpretation of the figures.','No universal increasing-accuracy rule follows.','k counts neighbors,not classes.','The aggregation rule changes even when data are fixed.'],typ='diagram')
